## Audit Limits

- No real account was created.
- No email was sent.
- No real or test payment was submitted.
- No authenticated dashboard, profile management, version history, export history, subscription management, connector, cancellation, refund, or deletion flow was available for verification.
- Visual inspection coered current desktop and a 390×844 mobile viewport, not the full device/browser matrix.
- Accessibility checks were limited to visible contrast/layout review and accessible DOM signals such as headings, roles, selected/pressed state, expanded navigation state, and form labels. This was not a full WCAG audit and did not include screen-reader testing, full keyboard-only testing, automated contrast measurement, zoom/reflow at 200–400%, or reduced-motion verification.
- Legal language was checked for internal consistency only; this is not legal advice or counsel review.
- The Littlebird comparison is based on publicly available official product, pricing, integration, and privacy materials rather than hands-on product testing.
- Direct-competitor classifications are based on publicly available official product and pricing materials. Creed, PersonalOS, CoreMem, Pecan, MultiPass, and Purpose were not independently tested hands-on in this audit.
- The assessment reflects the live site state observed on the audit date and may become stale after deployment.
